        : Extends
        :
..........................
: JdbcTransactionManager :
: (CLASS)                :  JdbcTransactionManager extends DataSourceTransactionManager and provides JDBC-specific, transaction handling, while DataSourceTransactionManager
:........................:  is the generic JDBC transaction manager.  Better support for: Exception translation, Declarative transactions.


Types of Transaction Manager :
         there are two types majorly :
                 - Declarative :
                             - transaction management through annotation.
                             - @Transactional.
                             - spring boot will choose appropriate transaction manager.
                             - we can create explicit transaction manager and tell spring to choose that.
                 - Programmatic :
                             - handle Transaction programmatically through code.
                             - flexible but difficult to maintain.
                             - which case to use this ? very specific case
                             - eg :  @Component
                                    public class User{
                                        @Transactional
                                        public void updateUser(){
                                            // 1. Update DB.
                                            // 2. External Api call through restTemplate.
                                            // 3. Update DB.
                                        }
                                    }
                            - there are two approches for programmatic .
                                                    - Using PlatformTransactionManager (Low-level / Manual):
                                                    - Using TransactionTemplate (Recommended way) :
